WEBVTT

00:00.210 --> 00:01.620
Instructor: All right, so in this video,

00:01.620 --> 00:04.710
I'm gonna demonstrate generating a merge conflict

00:04.710 --> 00:06.180
and then resolving it,

00:06.180 --> 00:09.960
and I'm gonna keep working with our simple repository.

00:09.960 --> 00:12.510
Currently, it has two branches, master and ABBA,

00:12.510 --> 00:14.760
but I'm actually gonna delete the ABBA branch

00:14.760 --> 00:16.680
because I merged in those changes,

00:16.680 --> 00:18.150
and let's say I'm done with it,

00:18.150 --> 00:20.070
so I'm gonna delete it.

00:20.070 --> 00:21.630
There's a couple ways of doing it.

00:21.630 --> 00:23.070
I've actually already shown this,

00:23.070 --> 00:26.820
but basically, git branch -d

00:26.820 --> 00:28.320
and then a branch name,

00:28.320 --> 00:30.510
and you wanna make sure you're not on that branch,

00:30.510 --> 00:33.300
so if I wanna delete this ABBA branch,

00:33.300 --> 00:35.640
I'm not on it, so git branch,

00:35.640 --> 00:39.063
I'll do a full screen, -d ABBA,

00:40.110 --> 00:41.640
and it's gone,

00:41.640 --> 00:44.340
so I had all the changes merged into master,

00:44.340 --> 00:46.140
so it doesn't warn me.

00:46.140 --> 00:48.630
When I first introduced how to delete a branch,

00:48.630 --> 00:49.530
it did warn us

00:49.530 --> 00:52.140
because we hadn't learned how to merge changes in,

00:52.140 --> 00:53.700
but now everything is merged in.

00:53.700 --> 00:56.850
I don't need to force this delete with a capital D.

00:56.850 --> 01:00.750
Okay, so now we have just the master branch, all right?

01:00.750 --> 01:04.650
So now what I'm going to do to demonstrate merge conflicts

01:04.650 --> 01:07.140
is I'm gonna make two branches, and I'll do it quickly.

01:07.140 --> 01:08.880
I'll probably fast forward through a lot of it.

01:08.880 --> 01:11.640
One for our friend Bjorn

01:11.640 --> 01:15.120
and another for our friend, I don't know, Serena,

01:15.120 --> 01:17.730
and they're going to each have their own branch

01:17.730 --> 01:20.580
where they can make their own playlist for the road trip,

01:20.580 --> 01:22.740
and they're definitely not going to agree,

01:22.740 --> 01:25.050
so they'll make their own playlist on their own branch,

01:25.050 --> 01:26.340
and then I'll merge them together

01:26.340 --> 01:28.050
when we're ready for our road trip,

01:28.050 --> 01:30.630
so I'll start by making Serena's branch,

01:30.630 --> 01:32.040
so I'll do it in one go:

01:32.040 --> 01:36.630
git switch -c serena, okay?

01:36.630 --> 01:41.630
And then I'll also go back to master, git switch master,

01:42.000 --> 01:43.620
and then I'll make the other branch,

01:43.620 --> 01:48.620
git switch -c for bjorn, all right?

01:49.380 --> 01:51.210
So now we have two branches.

01:51.210 --> 01:52.050
Well, we have three,

01:52.050 --> 01:54.990
but we have two that we just made, serena and bjorn,

01:54.990 --> 01:57.090
and they're all referring to the same spot

01:57.090 --> 01:59.010
that master currently is,

01:59.010 --> 02:01.170
so now we're gonna switch over.

02:01.170 --> 02:03.990
We're on bjorn, so let's just work on bjorn's branch.

02:03.990 --> 02:06.600
Bjorn really does not like ABBA that much,

02:06.600 --> 02:08.640
but he likes "Dancing Queen,"

02:08.640 --> 02:11.550
so he's gonna keep "Dancing Queen," okay?

02:11.550 --> 02:15.840
Then we're going to add some music in that Bjorn does like.

02:15.840 --> 02:18.810
Bjorn likes a band called King Gizzard &amp; the Lizard Wizard,

02:18.810 --> 02:20.640
so he adds that in.

02:20.640 --> 02:24.000
We'll make a commit for him, or he makes a commit.

02:24.000 --> 02:26.700
I'll just do it here. Stage all changes.

02:26.700 --> 02:31.530
Add, and I'm just gonna do King Gizzard Lizard Wizard song.

02:31.530 --> 02:35.550
All right, so we're on the bjorn branch,

02:35.550 --> 02:37.770
and he adds one more song.

02:37.770 --> 02:39.180
What should he do here?

02:39.180 --> 02:40.320
He likes the Strokes,

02:40.320 --> 02:44.460
so he adds both, or two songs in by the Strokes, okay?

02:44.460 --> 02:45.431
He stages them, he commits,

02:45.431 --> 02:49.980
add 2 Strokes songs, okay?

02:49.980 --> 02:54.690
Then, simultaneously, Serena is working on her branch,

02:54.690 --> 02:56.910
and she likes ABBA quite a bit.

02:56.910 --> 03:00.780
She even goes as far as to add another ABBA song in.

03:00.780 --> 03:05.780
She adds, what is it, "Gimme Gimme," I think, by ABBA.

03:06.270 --> 03:10.890
Okay, so she makes that commit, stages her change,

03:10.890 --> 03:13.593
add 1 ABBA song.

03:15.600 --> 03:18.630
Okay, and she does one more change.

03:18.630 --> 03:19.560
What else does she like?

03:19.560 --> 03:21.150
She likes Dolly Parton,

03:21.150 --> 03:24.360
so she adds, "Here You Come Again," okay?

03:24.360 --> 03:27.060
So she adds that change. She stages it.

03:27.060 --> 03:31.143
She commits add 1 dolly parton song.

03:32.310 --> 03:34.140
Okay, so now when we take a look,

03:34.140 --> 03:36.570
if we ignore everything that we did earlier,

03:36.570 --> 03:38.700
we just look from here and above,

03:38.700 --> 03:40.500
we can see that we have two branches.

03:40.500 --> 03:41.550
We're ignoring master.

03:41.550 --> 03:43.770
We have Serena and we have bjorn,

03:43.770 --> 03:48.090
and Serena has two commits that don't exist on bjorn,

03:48.090 --> 03:51.150
and bjorn has two commits that don't exist on Serena,

03:51.150 --> 03:54.300
but unlike the previous merge we did,

03:54.300 --> 03:56.820
where we were merging this ABBA branch

03:56.820 --> 03:58.200
with the master branch,

03:58.200 --> 03:59.700
there were no conflicts there.

03:59.700 --> 04:02.190
Here, there are definitely conflicts

04:02.190 --> 04:04.560
because we're editing the same file

04:04.560 --> 04:06.390
and some of the same lines,

04:06.390 --> 04:07.920
so when I switch, right?

04:07.920 --> 04:12.183
I'll switch one more time from Serena now to bjorn,

04:15.000 --> 04:17.940
we can see there's a lot of changes going on in there,

04:17.940 --> 04:20.310
so when I try and merge the two,

04:20.310 --> 04:21.810
we're gonna run into an issue,

04:21.810 --> 04:24.840
so now I have to decide where I want to do the merging.

04:24.840 --> 04:27.330
Do I want them to still have separate branches

04:27.330 --> 04:29.250
and just continue to have separate branches?

04:29.250 --> 04:32.130
If so, maybe I'll make a third branch.

04:32.130 --> 04:34.380
I'll call that one, what should it be?

04:34.380 --> 04:38.430
git switch -c combination, or just combo,

04:38.430 --> 04:40.380
and I'm branching from bjorn.

04:40.380 --> 04:41.610
That's where I am now,

04:41.610 --> 04:44.340
so it will include all the stuff from bjorn,

04:44.340 --> 04:48.330
and then I can merge in the changes from Serena.

04:48.330 --> 04:50.610
Okay, so now I have this new combo branch.

04:50.610 --> 04:52.980
It's at the same spot, right, as bjorn.

04:52.980 --> 04:54.690
They're referencing the same commit.

04:54.690 --> 04:57.900
Now I'm gonna merge in serena, so here we are.

04:57.900 --> 04:59.070
I'm on combo,

04:59.070 --> 05:01.380
which contains the same stuff as the bjorn branch.

05:01.380 --> 05:05.790
I'm gonna do git merge serena, and here we go.

05:05.790 --> 05:07.200
It tries to auto-merge.

05:07.200 --> 05:08.970
Nope. Conflict.

05:08.970 --> 05:11.310
Merge conflict in songs.txt.

05:11.310 --> 05:12.660
Automatic merge failed;

05:12.660 --> 05:15.450
fix conflicts, and then commit the result,

05:15.450 --> 05:17.100
so we go to our editor.

05:17.100 --> 05:18.600
I'm using VS Code.

05:18.600 --> 05:21.090
You can see it does some nice highlighting for me,

05:21.090 --> 05:23.460
and we have those markers I mentioned,

05:23.460 --> 05:25.830
so you can see HEAD right here.

05:25.830 --> 05:28.620
From that line down to here, those equal sign,

05:28.620 --> 05:31.620
this is what we had on the branch originally.

05:31.620 --> 05:34.950
In our case, it was the combo branch, so we can see it.

05:34.950 --> 05:38.610
It's bjorn's changes, and then here, this is the change

05:38.610 --> 05:41.400
or the changes we had coming in from the serena branch,

05:41.400 --> 05:45.000
and I have to decide: do I want just serena stuff?

05:45.000 --> 05:46.440
Do I want just bjorn's?

05:46.440 --> 05:48.090
No, I want both,

05:48.090 --> 05:52.320
so what I'm gonna do is I'm gonna delete these markers.

05:52.320 --> 05:56.940
We get rid of those, so all of that,

05:56.940 --> 05:58.920
and then I'm going to keep,

05:58.920 --> 06:00.060
you know where they have overlap,

06:00.060 --> 06:01.830
for example, "Dancing Queen" is on both of them,

06:01.830 --> 06:04.920
I don't want "Dancing Queen" twice, so I'm gonna do that,

06:04.920 --> 06:07.380
and otherwise, I think everything is unique.

06:07.380 --> 06:09.420
The point is it's up to me.

06:09.420 --> 06:12.000
It's totally up to me what I wanna keep and don't keep,

06:12.000 --> 06:14.310
and in this case, I mean, if we're doing a playlist,

06:14.310 --> 06:16.290
two friends, I guess it's fair,

06:16.290 --> 06:17.979
it's equitable to allow them both,

06:17.979 --> 06:21.420
just take both of their songs and combine them,

06:21.420 --> 06:23.430
but if I wanted to, I could say, you know what?

06:23.430 --> 06:25.080
I only like Serena's songs.

06:25.080 --> 06:28.290
I'm getting rid of you, bjorn, and I could do that.

06:28.290 --> 06:29.160
Could just get rid of that,

06:29.160 --> 06:32.310
say this is what we're going with, but I'm not going to.

06:32.310 --> 06:34.170
I'm gonna keep both of their songs in there,

06:34.170 --> 06:37.380
and I just removed the duplicate, which was "Dancing Queen,"

06:37.380 --> 06:39.000
so now I save,

06:39.000 --> 06:41.160
so go back to this guide here.

06:41.160 --> 06:44.460
First step, open the files. Second, edit the files.

06:44.460 --> 06:47.460
Third, remove the conflict markers. We did that.

06:47.460 --> 06:51.090
Fourth, add the changes and make a commit,

06:51.090 --> 06:54.450
so whoops, I need to go back to my terminal.

06:54.450 --> 06:55.890
We type git status,

06:55.890 --> 06:59.790
and it tells us we're on this branch combo, unmerged paths,

06:59.790 --> 07:03.510
and it tells us this songs.txt file has been modified,

07:03.510 --> 07:08.370
so now we just add the changes, okay?

07:08.370 --> 07:10.803
And then we commit, git commit -m,

07:10.803 --> 07:14.100
and we can just do something like "resolve conflicts,"

07:14.100 --> 07:15.510
or it's up to you, really,

07:15.510 --> 07:16.920
but I'll just do "resolve conflicts"

07:16.920 --> 07:18.780
to keep it short and simple,

07:18.780 --> 07:20.550
and that's what this commit is.

07:20.550 --> 07:21.900
This commit is us

07:21.900 --> 07:24.693
merging and resolving those conflicts, okay?

07:25.860 --> 07:29.580
So now let's head over to our little visualization here.

07:29.580 --> 07:32.010
It looks exactly the same as what we had earlier.

07:32.010 --> 07:33.630
It's the same process, right?

07:33.630 --> 07:36.840
We merged this branch, serena, into combo,

07:36.840 --> 07:38.940
and we have this new merge commit.

07:38.940 --> 07:41.400
The difference is that we had to do some work

07:41.400 --> 07:42.600
to make that commit.

07:42.600 --> 07:44.550
We didn't just approve a commit message,

07:44.550 --> 07:46.290
like we did a couple videos ago.

07:46.290 --> 07:48.900
Instead, we actually had to dig into a file

07:48.900 --> 07:50.250
and make some changes.

07:50.250 --> 07:51.870
We had to look at those markers

07:51.870 --> 07:54.660
that get adds for us, these things,

07:54.660 --> 07:58.170
and figure out what we wanted to keep from the two branches

07:58.170 --> 08:01.980
and then make changes, save, and then add and commit,

08:01.980 --> 08:03.960
but now that conflict has been resolved,

08:03.960 --> 08:05.970
and we're on our new branch combo,

08:05.970 --> 08:07.950
which includes the commits that it had earlier,

08:07.950 --> 08:10.830
from bjorn and the new commits from serena

08:10.830 --> 08:13.443
and the conflicts there that we manually resolved.
